        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758303,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Nintendo 3DS is a foldable, dual-screen handheld game console that succeeded the Nintendo DS and DSi, released in 2011. A defining feature is its autostereoscopic 3D visuals, eliminating the need for special glasses. It retains backward compatibility with Nintendo DS software. Initially priced at $249.99, a subsequent price reduction and free game promotion significantly boosted its popularity. \n\nHardware revisions included the 3DS XL with larger screens, the 2DS (a non-folding model), and the New 3DS with upgraded hardware. The console boasts a virtual console library, Miis, an Activity Log, and the innovative StreetPass and SpotPass features. Popular titles include *Mario Kart 7*, which sold nearly 19 million units, alongside *Animal Crossing: New Leaf*, *The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time 3D*, and *Super Street Fighter IV 3D Edition*. Discontinued in 2020, the 3DS remains a beloved handheld."
          },
